---
/**
 * index.astro — the wicked-studio landing page (ws.wickedagile.com).
 *
 * POSITIONING: studio is the ADE (agentic development environment) for running a team of coding
 * agents. The page leads with that and
 * shows it: the hero IS a working miniature of the Desk (your jobs on the left, a job as a chat in
 * the middle, what changed on the right). Separate-agent review is a supporting proof further down,
 * not the hook.
 *
 * SHAPE: one job runs through the whole page. The hero's job, "Rate limits for the public API", is
 * the sample in every section after it: its plan and gate (the benefits), its pages (the sidebar
 * explorer), Codex's per-API-key finding and the receipt (review), the note it leaves (memory), the
 * files it touched (knowledge), its sandbox (agents). Each section is one frame on a desktop window
 * and carries one thing you can watch or drive. Frames: hook + demo → what it does for you → the
 * sidebar → a different agent checks → rules / memory / knowledge → agents + projects → what's new
 * in 0.16 → the platform map → get it.
 *
 * MOTION: every scene plays only while it is on screen, pauses on hover or focus, has a visible
 * Pause button where it loops, and shows its final state under prefers-reduced-motion. Every state a
 * scene or a control can reach is laid out up front (one grid cell per stack, fixed heights), so no
 * hover, focus, tap or animation moves anything outside its own box (src/scripts/page.js).
 *
 * ACCURACY (studio 0.16 / crew 0.18.0, the ui-v3 line). Every label in the demo is a real studio label:
 *  - A job's page is a chat: your messages right-aligned, each agent's turn under its name, the
 *    plan card's "Approve plan" / "Not now", one "Working on Build…" line, and the final message
 *    "Done. Tests pass (38), and codex reviewed and approved it. Pull request #12 is open." with
 *    the pull request, Changes and Evidence as chips (CHANGELOG 0.10.0).
 *  - Gate choices: "Approve", "Approve with a note for the next step", "Send back"
 *    (src/components/session/GateRow.tsx, gateMoveModel.ts).
 *  - A question card names the agent that asked (0.9.3). "Needs you" is the inbox (0.10.0).
 *  - Sidebar pages = NAV_GROUPS (Work: Projects, Jobs, Apps, Repositories, then Data sources when crew
 *    serves them; Insight: Report, Understand, Evaluate; Govern: Steering, Memory, Agents) + LEARN_ITEM at
 *    the rail's foot, above Build & settings, with no "Start here" mark (src/board/navModel.ts; names:
 *    src/board/pageNames.ts). The explorer and the demo strip list them in that order.
 *  - What's new in 0.16 (CHANGELOG [0.16.0], crew 0.18.0, DES-CATALOG-002 rev 8): documents as a job input
 *    (chat attachments: pdf, text, images; on Respond/Rework a pdf with no usable text is struck with its reason and
 *    Start waits; Respond = RFP/RFI/questionnaire, Rework = condense/re-audience/
 *    generalize/convert/refresh; a fidelity check before landing, a FAIL never lands silently); the per-job source
 *    pick (the sources token in JobPassage, swap list, a switched-off source is unpickable; units query only the
 *    picked registered sources, while the repository graph, rules and mcp:estate stay available);
 *    the sourced-report cards (research, competitive, due diligence, analyze documents, critique, estimate: claims
 *    cite sources, re-checked); review-change (seats that wrote none of it; nothing posted to the PR); apps publish
 *    (Share -> Publish sheet; signed-in viewers by default; check + QE + consent; local container image, docker run
 *    line, embed snippet only for a public app with no actions; wicked deploys nothing); phase plugins (the observe
 *    tier: "From plugin · <name>" in every job's Details; consent per event topic; Plugins lists it with off and
 *    Remove); run cost (comparable terminal runs, 90 days, median/p75/p90); demo video review/record again/edit/export
 *    (plugins S4; a demo whose app data stays out of model context gets no model review: the person reviews it). Not in it: plugin intercept hooks, Teams publishing. Nothing unreleased is named (operator rule
 *    2026-11-05).
 *  - Themes: Wicked Light, Wicked Dark, Ambient (src/theming/appearance.ts, AppearanceSettings.tsx).
 *  - Voice: the mic beside Send when crew has voice, local transcription (src/components/voice/).
 *    Wherever voice appears, the N6 line sits beside it.
 *  - Review on the builder's own agent is refused unless the job is launched with reduced
 *    assurance, labelled on the job, every gate and the delivery (crew 0.9.0 / core-ts 0.7.46).
 *  - The assurance receipt: required vs ran, who built / reviewed / judged, what was skipped.
 *  - QE acceptance is required for feature / bug / migration / mcp-server / editor-plugin launches,
 *    unless a labelled waiver (lowest score on every measure) or a skip with a reason (core
 *    src/catalog.rs builtin_preset_instruments).
 *  - Rules apply to every repository or to one project and can target a language, layer or
 *    framework; there is no per-repo target (core crates/wicked-governance/src/conformance.rs).
 *  - Studio grades nothing: the checks are crew's, the store is estate's. Studio is a pure client
 *    of crew's /api/v1 + /ws; the wire contract wicked-crew-api-types is the only shared code.
 * Never hardcode the installed version in prose: the install stamp is injected at build time (DT-7).
 * The one exception is the "What's new in 0.16" frame, which names the release it describes.
 * Schematics in the sidebar explorer are labelled "illustration"; the search table is labelled an
 * example. No numbers appear apart from the demo's and the example table's.
 */
import Base from 'wicked-web/layouts/Base.astro';
import Topbar from 'wicked-web/components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from 'wicked-web/components/Footer.astro';
import SameGarden from 'wicked-web/components/SameGarden.astro';
import '../styles/studio.css';

// The hook (messaging N2). Kept as strings so the operator can swap a variant in one place. ADE is
// spelled out on first use: the kicker above the headline reads it in full, and the headline's
// <abbr> carries the expansion for assistive tech.
const ABBR = 'ADE';
const ABBR_FULL = 'agentic development environment';
const KICKER = 'Agentic development environment (ADE)';
const HEADLINE = 'The ADE for running a team of coding agents.';
const [HEAD_PRE, HEAD_POST] = HEADLINE.split(ABBR);
const SUBLINE = 'Chat with them, or talk to them. Watch the work happen, make the calls only you can make, and ship what they changed.';
// The default-review qualifier (messaging N1), as small print on the first screen.
const FINE =
  'By default a different agent reviews the work. When none can, the job stops unless you launch it as “reduced assurance”, which is labelled on the job, every gate and the delivery. A saved workflow may require fewer checks; its requirements are listed in the receipts.';
// The voice privacy line (messaging N6), beside every mention of voice.
const VOICE = 'Speech is turned into text on your machine, and the audio is never stored.';

const title = 'wicked-studio — the ADE for running a team of coding agents';
// What search results and social cards show. Same attribution boundary as the page: the crew
// daemon runs the agents; studio is the screen you run them from.
const description =
  'The agentic development environment (ADE) for running a team of coding agents. Chat with Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, OpenCode and Pi, watch the work happen live, answer the gates that need you, and approve what changed. Build apps and dashboards over your data by chat, and decide what agents may read from each source. By default a different agent reviews every change, and the wicked-crew daemon on your machine runs each agent in a sandbox.';
const repo = 'https://github.com/mikeparcewski/wicked-studio';

// The sidebar's real pages (NAV_GROUPS + LEARN_ITEM in src/board/navModel.ts), one plain line each.
const TABS = [
  { name: 'Projects', line: 'Group repos and jobs; one code graph over the repos.' },
  { name: 'Jobs', line: 'Every job as one chat, with the gates you answer.' },
  { name: 'Apps', line: 'Dashboards and small tools over your data, built by chat.' },
  { name: 'Repositories', line: 'Code graphs, and how much is mapped to requirements.' },
  { name: 'Data sources', line: 'Your databases, APIs, files and trackers, and what agents may read.' },
  { name: 'Report', line: 'How the work went, and the dashboards you choose to show.' },
  { name: 'Understand', line: 'Ask how your code fits together. Answers cite the code.' },
  { name: 'Evaluate', line: 'Test your rules against examples first.' },
  { name: 'Steering', line: 'Your rules: everywhere or one project, by language, layer or framework.' },
  { name: 'Memory', line: 'What happened, what you said, what jobs learned.' },
  { name: 'Agents', line: 'Sign each agent in once. It runs in a sandbox.' },
  { name: 'Learn', line: 'Teach it how you work: docs, rules, personality, brand.' },
];
const line = (n: string) => TABS.find((t) => t.name === n)!.line;
// The sidebar's own groups (navModel.ts NAV_GROUPS), then Learn at the rail's foot, above Build & settings.
const GROUPS = [
  { label: 'Work', items: ['Projects', 'Jobs', 'Apps', 'Repositories', 'Data sources'] },
  { label: 'Insight', items: ['Report', 'Understand', 'Evaluate'] },
  { label: 'Govern', items: ['Steering', 'Memory', 'Agents'] },
  { label: '', items: ['Learn'] },
];
// The page the explorer opens on.
const FIRST = 'Projects';
// On a desktop window each group's heading sits beside its pages (one grid row per page), so the
// twelve pages fit the frame: the grid row each group starts on.
const ROW = GROUPS.map((_, i) => 1 + GROUPS.slice(0, i).reduce((a, x) => a + x.items.length, 0));
const slug = (n: string) => n.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-');

const AGENTS = ['Claude Code', 'Codex', 'GitHub Copilot', 'OpenCode', 'Pi'];

// The page's spine (the same thread and beat track as wicked-crew's): the hero, then the frames that
// follow its job. Each beat is named from its own frame's kicker or heading. What's new, the platform
// map and Get it are not beats.
const BEATS = [
  { id: 'top', name: 'The ADE' },
  { id: 'why', name: 'For you' },
  { id: 'desk', name: 'Desk' },
  { id: 'review', name: 'Review' },
  { id: 'steer', name: 'Rules' },
  { id: 'reach', name: 'Agents' },
];

// Three benefits, right under the demo (studio 0.16 / crew 0.18.0).
const BENEFITS = [
  { h: 'Start with a chat, not a form.', p: 'Describe what you want; the chat proposes a plan, and nothing starts until you confirm it.' },
  { h: 'Gate decisions come to you as one card.', p: 'The card shows the choices, marks the recommended one when there is one, and, when given, what each would do. Confirm, then undo within 10 seconds if you change your mind.' },
  { h: 'It learns how you work.', p: 'Learn turns your team docs, your best repos and your writing into suggested rules and memories, and sets the tone the lead agent takes with you. You choose which suggestions become active.' },
];

// What's new in 0.16, one line each. `tab` is the item's short name on its tab (the row stays one line at
// every width); the panel's heading carries the full name and labels the panel. Each item is one shipped piece of
// the release (DES-CATALOG-002 rev 8 CS2-CS12, plugins S4); an item is cut, never softened, if it did not ship.
const NEW = [
  { name: 'Documents in a job', tab: 'Documents', line: 'Attach PDFs, text or images in the chat, and the job’s sentence lists them. Respond answers an RFP, RFI or questionnaire from them; Rework makes a new document from them.',
    more: 'A PDF with no readable text (a scan) is set aside, with the reason. A fidelity check runs before either lands, and a failed check never lands silently.' },
  { name: 'Sources you pick', tab: 'Sources', line: 'A job that reads data sources names them in its sentence: “reading the web and support-pg”. Tap it to swap from your project’s sources, the web included. Its agents query only the sources you picked; your repository keeps its usual access.',
    more: 'A source whose “Agents can query” switch is off cannot be picked, and the job says so.' },
  { name: 'Reports with sources', tab: 'Reports', line: 'Research, Competitive, Due diligence, Analyze documents, Critique and Estimate return a report where every claim cites its source, and a check re-reads each claim at that source before you see it.' },
  { name: 'Review a change', tab: 'Review', line: 'Type /review-change and a pull request link. You get approve, conditional or reject, with cited findings, judged by agents that wrote none of the change. Nothing is posted to the pull request.' },
  { name: 'Publish an app', tab: 'Publish', line: 'Publish from an app’s Share sheet: choose who can see it (signed-in viewers by default), and crew checks it, runs QE and asks for your consent before it builds the container image on your machine.',
    more: 'You get the image, its docker run line and, for a public app (every query public, no actions), an embed snippet. You run it where you choose.' },
  { name: 'Phase plugins', tab: 'Plugins', line: 'Type /plugin phase and what you want to see. It builds a plugin that adds a section to every job’s details, drawn from the job’s events.',
    more: 'Installing it asks you to approve each event topic it reads. Plugins lists it, with off and Remove.' },
  { name: 'Run cost', tab: 'Run cost', line: 'Ask what 40 bug fixes a month would cost. The answer comes from your own comparable runs (median, p75 and p90 spend and time), with every assumption named.' },
  { name: 'Demo videos you can review', tab: 'Demo video', line: 'A demo video’s review gate shows who reviewed the take, what they found and its contact sheets; a demo whose app data stays out of model context is reviewed by you. Record it again with a note, then edit the cut and export it as a video, a GIF or a poster.' },
];

// The example search in the projects card: one project, three repos.
const HITS = [
  { repo: 'wicked-core', n: 4, lang: 'Rust' },
  { repo: 'wicked-crew', n: 3, lang: 'TypeScript' },
  { repo: 'wicked-studio', n: 1, lang: 'TypeScript' },
];
// page.js alternates the search between these (same repos, same labels: an example).
const QUERIES = [
  { q: 'register', n: HITS.map((h) => h.n) },
  { q: 'rateLimit', n: [2, 3, 1] },
];

// Injected at build time from the repo's package.json via astro.config.mjs (DT-7).
const studioVersion = __WICKED_STUDIO_VERSION__;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Topbar pkg="wicked-studio" repo={repo} />

  {/* The spine, at 1024px wide and up: the job's beats as one thread under the topbar, filling as each
      beat arrives (decoration; the beat track says it in words). */}
  <div class="beat-thread" data-beat-thread aria-hidden="true">{BEATS.map((b) => <i data-beat-thread-seg={b.id}><b></b></i>)}</div>

  {/* The spine: the job's beats, in the right gutter (1400px wide and up, where the gutter holds it). */}
  <nav class="beats" data-beats aria-label="The job, beat by beat">
    <ol>
      {BEATS.map((b, i) => (
        <li><a href={`#${b.id}`} data-beat-link={b.id}><span class="beats-l">{b.name}</span><span class="beats-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sr-only">{`, beat ${i + 1} of ${BEATS.length}`}</span></a></li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </nav>

  {/* ── 1. Hook + the working demo ───────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="hero frame snap-section" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div class="amber-floor" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero-wrap">
      {/* the narrowest phones (under 360px): the header's path cuts the package name short, so the hero names it */}
      <p class="hero-pkg" aria-hidden="true">wicked-studio</p>
      <div class="hero-head">
        <p class="kicker beat hero-kick">{KICKER}</p>
        <h1 id="hero-h">{HEAD_PRE}<abbr title={ABBR_FULL}>{ABBR}</abbr>{HEAD_POST}</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="lede">{SUBLINE}</p>
          <div class="hero-agents">
            <p class="mini-k" id="hero-agents-k">Bring the agents you already use</p>
            <ul class="agent-row" role="list" aria-labelledby="hero-agents-k">
              {AGENTS.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-cta">
            <button class="cta-copy" type="button" data-copy="npx wicked-crew serve" aria-label="Copy npx wicked-crew serve">
              <span class="cta-prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span><code>npx wicked-crew serve</code><span class="cta-copy-l" data-copy-label aria-hidden="true">Copy</span>
            </button>
            <p class="cta-alt">One command on your machine starts the wicked-crew daemon, which runs your agents in sandboxes, and serves studio in your browser. <a href="#demo" class="cta-watch" data-watch>Watch a job<span class="cta-arr" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></p>
          </div>
          <p class="voice-note hero-voice"><span class="mic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Voice needs whisper.cpp. {VOICE}</span></p>
          <p class="hero-fine">{FINE}</p>
        </div>

        {/* A working miniature of the Desk. Left: your jobs. Middle: the selected job as a chat.
             Right: what changed, and the job's receipt. Scripted, not live: it never calls a daemon
             (src/scripts/demo.js). */}
        <div class="ide" id="demo" data-ide role="region" aria-label="A working demo of wicked-studio: three jobs, one of them yours to drive">
          <div class="ide-bar">
            <span class="ide-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <nav class="ide-tabs" aria-label="Sidebar pages (illustration)">
              <span>Projects</span> <span class="is-on">Jobs</span> <span>Apps</span> <span>Repositories</span> <span>Data sources</span> <span>Report</span> <span>Understand</span> <span>Evaluate</span> <span>Steering</span> <span>Memory</span> <span>Agents</span> <span>Learn</span>
            </nav>
            <span class="ide-url" data-demo-note>scripted demo · approve the plan, then make the calls</span>
            <button type="button" class="play-toggle play-toggle--sm" data-play-toggle data-demo-pause aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause the demo's motion"><span class="pt-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pt-l" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pt-pause">Pause</span><span class="pt-play">Play</span></span></button>
          </div>

          <div class="ide-body">
            <aside class="ide-rail" aria-label="Your jobs">
              <div class="ide-rail-top">
                <button type="button" class="ide-new" data-act="restart">+ New job</button>
                <p class="ide-rail-k">Needs you <span class="ide-count" data-needs>1</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="ide-sessions" role="tablist" aria-label="Jobs" aria-orientation="vertical" data-sessions></div>
            </aside>

            <div class="ide-main" id="ide-main" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ide-tab-rate">
              <div class="ide-head">
                <span class="ide-title" data-title>Rate limits for the public API</span>
                <ol class="ide-steps" data-steps aria-label="Steps"></ol>
              </div>
              <div class="ide-thread" data-thread role="log" tabindex="-1" aria-live="polite" aria-label="The job's conversation"></div>
              <form class="ide-composer" data-composer>
                <input type="text" data-input aria-label="Message your agents" placeholder="Message your agents…" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                       value="Add rate limiting to the public API: 100 requests a minute per API key." />
                <button type="submit" class="ide-send" data-send>Send</button>
              </form>
            </div>

            <aside class="ide-pane" aria-label="What changed">
              <div class="ide-pane-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Side panel">
                <button type="button" role="tab" id="ide-ptab-changes" class="is-on" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="ide-pane-body" tabindex="0" data-pane-tab="changes">Changes <span class="ide-count ide-count--quiet" data-files>0</span></button>
                <button type="button" role="tab" id="ide-ptab-receipt" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="ide-pane-body" tabindex="-1" data-pane-tab="receipt">Receipt</button>
              </div>
              <div class="ide-pane-body" id="ide-pane-body" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ide-ptab-changes" tabindex="0" data-pane></div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── 2. What studio does for you: three benefits, each a short scene from the same job ── */}
  <section class="why frame snap-section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h" data-autoplay>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head sec-head--row">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker beat">Example job: rate limits for the public API</p>
          <h2 id="why-h">What studio does for you</h2>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="play-toggle" data-play-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause the scenes"><span class="pt-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pt-l" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pt-pause">Pause</span><span class="pt-play">Play</span></span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="trio ben-row" data-swipe>
        {BENEFITS.map((b, i) => (
          <div class={`trio-card ben ben--${'abc'[i]}`}>
            <div class={`scene scene-${'abc'[i]} st-1 st-2 st-3 st-4`} data-scene={'abc'[i]} data-step="4" aria-hidden="true">
              {i === 0 && (
                <div class="scene-in">
                  <div class="sa-user">Add rate limiting to the public API: 100 requests a minute per API key.</div>
                  <div class="sa-stack">
                    <p class="sa-work"><span class="pulse"></span>Claude Code is planning…</p>
                    <div class="sa-plan">
                      <span class="s-who">Claude Code</span>
                      <p>Here is my plan. Nothing starts until you approve it.</p>
                      <ol><li>Build: a rate-limit middleware</li><li>Review: <b>Codex</b> checks it, not me</li><li>Test: run the suite</li><li>Deliver: open a pull request</li></ol>
                      <div class="s-acts"><span class="s-btn s-btn--yes sa-ok">Approve plan</span><span class="s-btn">Not now</span></div>
                      <p class="s-decided sa-done">You approved the plan.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              )}
              {i === 1 && (
                <div class="scene-in">
                  <div class="sb-card">
                    <span class="s-who">Gate · Codex reviewed the build</span>
                    <p>One finding: the limit is keyed on the client IP, but you asked for a limit <b>per API key</b>.</p>
                    <div class="sb-opts">
                      <span class="sb-opt">Approve</span>
                      <span class="sb-opt">Approve with a note</span>
                      <span class="sb-opt sb-opt--rec">Send back <i>Recommended</i></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="sb-foot">
                      <span class="s-btn s-btn--yes sb-confirm">Confirm</span>
                      <span class="sb-undo"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8" class="sb-ring-bg"></circle><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8" class="sb-ring"></circle></svg><span>Sent back. <u>Undo</u></span></span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              )}
              {i === 2 && (
                <div class="scene-in">
                  <div class="sc-src"><span>Team docs</span><span>Best repos</span><span>Your writing</span></div>
                  <div class="sc-flow"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                  <ul class="sc-list">
                    <li class="sc-item sc-1"><span class="sc-k">Rule</span><span class="sc-t">Public routes carry a rate limit</span><span class="sc-tog"></span></li>
                    <li class="sc-item sc-2"><span class="sc-k">Memory</span><span class="sc-t">Limits are per API key</span><span class="sc-tog"></span></li>
                    <li class="sc-item sc-3"><span class="sc-k">Tone</span><span class="sc-t">Short answers, plain words</span><span class="sc-tog"></span></li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              )}
            </div>
            <h3>{b.h}</h3>
            <p>{b.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="swipe-dots" data-swipe-dots aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── 3. The sidebar, explorable: the whole surface at a glance ─────────── */}
  <section class="desk frame snap-section" id="desk" aria-labelledby="desk-h" data-autoplay>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head sec-head--row">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker beat">Same job, in the Desk</p>
          <h2 id="desk-h">One Desk for every agent and every repo.</h2>
          <p class="sec-sub">The Desk is studio’s one screen: launch jobs across your projects and let them run. When one needs a decision, it comes to you.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="play-toggle" data-play-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause the tour of the pages"><span class="pt-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pt-l" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pt-pause">Pause</span><span class="pt-play">Play</span></span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="explorer" data-tour data-tour-ms="4000">
        <div class="ex-side" role="tablist" aria-label="Sidebar pages" aria-orientation="vertical">
          {GROUPS.map((g, gi) => (
            <>
              {g.label && <span class="ex-group" aria-hidden="true" style={`grid-row: ${ROW[gi]} / span ${g.items.length}`}>{g.label}</span>}
              {g.items.map((n, k) => (
