  {/* ── 4. A different agent checks the work: the relay, and the receipt it leaves ── */}
  <section class="review frame snap-section" id="review" aria-labelledby="review-h" data-relay data-autoplay>
    <div class="wrap review-grid">
      <div class="review-left">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <p class="kicker beat">Example job: rate limits for the public API · Build, Review, You</p>
          <h2 id="review-h">A different agent checks the work.</h2>
          <p class="sec-sub">By default a different agent reviews the change. A gate’s receipt names who built, reviewed and judged it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="relay has-arc" data-mode="two" data-tok="y">
          <ol class="flow" aria-label="Who does what on a job">
            <li class="fl-b" data-s="s2"><span class="flow-who">Builder</span><span class="flow-what">Claude Code writes the change in its sandbox</span><span class="fl-s" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fl-s1">writing</span><span class="fl-s2">fixed: per API key</span><span class="fl-s3">built</span></span></li>
            <li class="fl-r" data-s="s2"><span class="flow-who">Reviewer</span><span class="flow-what">Codex checks it, and can send it back</span><span class="fl-s" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fl-s1">one finding</span><span class="fl-s2">approved</span><span class="fl-s3">no second agent</span></span></li>
            <li class="fl-y is-lit" data-s="s2"><span class="flow-who flow-who--you">You</span><span class="flow-what">approve, add a note, or send it back</span><span class="fl-s" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fl-s2">approved</span></span></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="relay-track" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="relay-arc" viewBox="0 0 20 100" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M15 96 C -3 78, -3 22, 15 4" /></svg>
            <span class="relay-token"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts" role="list">
          <li>Only one agent signed in? The job stops and says why, unless you launch it with <b>reduced assurance</b>, labelled everywhere.</li>
          <li>Jobs launched as a feature, bug fix, migration, MCP server or editor plugin need <b>acceptance testing (QE)</b> before they ship. A change small on every measure is waived, and skipping takes a reason; either is labelled.</li>
          <li>The checks are <a href="https://wc.wickedagile.com">crew’s</a>. Studio shows them and never grades anything.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="review-right">
        <div class="relay-ctl">
          <button type="button" class="switch" role="switch" aria-checked="true" aria-label="Two agents signed in" data-relay-switch>
            <span class="switch-track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
            <span class="switch-l" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sw-on">Two agents signed in</span><span class="sw-off">Only one agent signed in</span></span>
          </button>
          <span class="relay-btns"><button type="button" class="play-toggle" data-play-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause the replays"><span class="pt-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pt-l" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pt-pause">Pause</span><span class="pt-play">Play</span></span></button><button type="button" class="replay" data-relay-replay>Replay</button></span>
        </div>
        <figure class="receipt" aria-label="An example assurance receipt" data-mode="two">
          <figcaption>Receipt · job r-7c19 · build step</figcaption>
          <table>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="is-filled" data-row="1"><th scope="row">Required</th><td><span class="rv rv-two">tests pass, a different agent reviews</span><span class="rv rv-one">tests pass, a different agent reviews</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="is-filled" data-row="4"><th scope="row">Ran</th><td><span class="rv rv-two">tests (38 pass), review</span><span class="rv rv-one">the build; then the job held at review</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="is-filled" data-row="1"><th scope="row">Built by</th><td><span class="rv rv-two">Claude Code</span><span class="rv rv-one">Claude Code</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="is-filled" data-row="4"><th scope="row">Reviewed by</th><td><span class="rv rv-two">Codex <span class="ok">separate agent</span></span><span class="rv rv-one">nobody yet: no second agent</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="is-filled" data-row="5"><th scope="row">Skipped</th><td><span class="rv rv-two">nothing</span><span class="rv rv-one">nothing: the job waits</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <div class="rc-foot">
            <p class="receipt-foot">“Passed checks, nobody reviewed it” never reads like “independently accepted”.</p>
            <p class="relay-stop"><b>Held.</b> Only one agent is signed in, so no other agent can review the change. Sign in a second agent, or launch it again as reduced assurance; the label goes on the job, every gate and the delivery.</p>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

